{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "framework-edge-quantize-fp8",
      "prompt": "Quantize nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge to FP8 on this machine's single GPU with the skill's documented DEMO=1 recipe (the Edge section of the Edge/Nano/Super notebook: one calibration prompt at the small shape, profile t2v, the video base sampler). Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Write the FP8 checkpoint to a scratch directory outside the artifacts dir (it is roughly the size of the bf16 source), run the notebook's 'Inspect the FP8 Checkpoint' step on it and save the printed summary as outputs/edge-fp8-inspect.txt, and copy the checkpoint's root hf_quant_config.json to outputs/edge-fp8-hf_quant_config.json. Do not run the Nano or Super sections.",
      "expected_outcome": "An FP8 drop-in checkpoint for Cosmos3-Edge is written by quantize_fp8_checkpoint (DEMO=1) from a fresh clone of the public framework main, its inspect summary (quant_algo FP8, non-zero FP8 weight and scale-tensor counts) is in outputs/edge-fp8-inspect.txt next to a copy of hf_quant_config.json, and result_summary.md records the run facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The framework checkout is a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main (the transcript shows the clone), set up with the skill's documented uv sync and the ModelOpt 0.44.0 install into that venv",
        "quantize_fp8_checkpoint ran for nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge with profile t2v, SAMPLER_VIDEO_BASE, the DEMO shape and one calibration sample, as the Edge section documents, and no Nano or Super run was started",
        "outputs/edge-fp8-inspect.txt holds the inspect_checkpoint summary of the written checkpoint - quant_algo FP8 (method modelopt), a non-zero count of FP8 weights and of scale tensors - produced by the run recorded in the transcript (not fabricated)",
        "outputs/edge-fp8-hf_quant_config.json is a copy of the hf_quant_config.json written at the checkpoint root, and the checkpoint itself was written outside the artifacts dir",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records the checkpoint directory, the DEMO setting and shape, the wall-clock time of the quantization and the peak GPU memory observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/edge-fp8-inspect.txt",
          "contains": "FP8 weights"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/edge-fp8-inspect.txt",
          "contains": "quant_algo   : FP8"
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/edge-fp8-hf_quant_config.json",
          "contains": "quant_algo"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "calibrate + export (Edge, DEMO=1)",
        "inspect",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "framework-super-t2i-quantize-fp8",
      "prompt": "Quantize the Cosmos3-Super Text-to-Image models to FP8 with the skill's documented DEMO=1 recipe on this machine's single GPU: the base model (nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Text2Image, profile t2i, the image base sampler) first, then the 4-step distilled student (nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Text2Image-4Step, the distilled sampler). Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Write the checkpoints to a scratch directory outside the artifacts dir; for each one that completes, run the notebook's inspect step and save the printed summary as outputs/super-t2i-fp8-inspect.txt and outputs/super-t2i-distilled-fp8-inspect.txt. The recipe loads the full bf16 checkpoint of a 64B-class model even with DEMO=1 (the notebook: the run 'needs a GPU with enough memory to hold the model in bf16 plus the quantizers'). First compare the base checkpoint's bf16 size from Hub metadata (HfApi().model_info(..., files_metadata=True)) with the GPU memory nvidia-smi reports on this machine: if the checkpoint alone exceeds the GPU, that measured comparison is the blocker - record both numbers in result_summary.md and do not download the checkpoint or attempt the 4-step student (record the same blocker for it). Only if it fits, make a genuine attempt and, if that attempt fails, record the exact error with the measured memory numbers. Never fabricate a checkpoint or an inspect summary.",
      "expected_outcome": "FP8 checkpoints and inspect summaries for the Super Text-to-Image base and 4-step models exist in artifacts; only if real quantization attempts on this GPU fail does result_summary.md instead document the precise blocker with measured numbers.",
      "assertions": [
        "The run produced outputs/super-t2i-fp8-inspect.txt and outputs/super-t2i-distilled-fp8-inspect.txt from completed quantize_fp8_checkpoint runs, or documented the concrete blocker with measured evidence: the base checkpoint's bf16 size from Hub metadata against the GPU memory nvidia-smi reports (and, when the checkpoint fits and a real attempt was made, the exact error)",
        "No output was fabricated: any inspect summary present traces to a real quantize_fp8_checkpoint run recorded in the transcript",
        "The documented recipe was followed from a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main set up per the skill: profile t2i, SAMPLER_IMAGE_BASE for the base model and SAMPLER_DISTILLED for the student, DEMO=1, OUTPUT_ROOT outside the checkout",
        "The skill's documented setup and recipe steps executed without errors on the first attempt up to the GPU memory limit, if one was hit; no documented command needed a self-correction",
        "result_summary.md states the GPU memory available versus the checkpoint's bf16 size and, for any completed checkpoint, the inspect summary facts"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "quantize attempt or blocker analysis",
        "summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "framework-super-i2v-quantize-fp8",
      "prompt": "Quantize the Cosmos3-Super Image-to-Video models to FP8 with the skill's documented DEMO=1 recipe on this machine's single GPU: the base model (nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Image2Video, profile i2v, the video base sampler) first, then the 4-step distilled student (nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Image2Video-4Step, the distilled sampler). Provide the conditioning images the recipe needs through I2V_COND_DIR (a local folder with at least one real image; a small public image downloaded for this run is fine - say which) or rely on the notebook's dataset fallback, and record the choice. Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Write the checkpoints to a scratch directory outside the artifacts dir; for each one that completes, run the notebook's inspect step and save the printed summary as outputs/super-i2v-fp8-inspect.txt and outputs/super-i2v-distilled-fp8-inspect.txt. The recipe loads the full bf16 checkpoint of a 64B-class model even with DEMO=1 (the notebook: the run 'needs a GPU with enough memory to hold the model in bf16 plus the quantizers'). First compare the base checkpoint's bf16 size from Hub metadata (HfApi().model_info(..., files_metadata=True)) with the GPU memory nvidia-smi reports on this machine: if the checkpoint alone exceeds the GPU, that measured comparison is the blocker - record both numbers in result_summary.md and do not download the checkpoint or attempt the 4-step student (record the same blocker for it). Only if it fits, make a genuine attempt and, if that attempt fails, record the exact error with the measured memory numbers. Never fabricate a checkpoint or an inspect summary.",
      "expected_outcome": "FP8 checkpoints and inspect summaries for the Super Image-to-Video base and 4-step models exist in artifacts; only if real quantization attempts on this GPU fail does result_summary.md instead document the precise blocker with measured numbers.",
      "assertions": [
        "The run produced outputs/super-i2v-fp8-inspect.txt and outputs/super-i2v-distilled-fp8-inspect.txt from completed quantize_fp8_checkpoint runs, or documented the concrete blocker with measured evidence: the base checkpoint's bf16 size from Hub metadata against the GPU memory nvidia-smi reports (and, when the checkpoint fits and a real attempt was made, the exact error)",
        "No output was fabricated: any inspect summary present traces to a real quantize_fp8_checkpoint run recorded in the transcript",
        "The documented recipe was followed from a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main set up per the skill: profile i2v with the conditioning-image choice recorded, SAMPLER_VIDEO_BASE for the base model and SAMPLER_DISTILLED for the student, DEMO=1, OUTPUT_ROOT outside the checkout",
        "The skill's documented setup and recipe steps executed without errors on the first attempt up to the GPU memory limit, if one was hit; no documented command needed a self-correction",
        "result_summary.md states the GPU memory available versus the checkpoint's bf16 size and, for any completed checkpoint, the inspect summary facts"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "conditioning images",
        "quantize attempt or blocker analysis",
        "summarize"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
